This repository includes third-party software:

- Desktop UI (`packages/app`, `packages/desktop`, `packages/ui`,
  `packages/session-ui`, `packages/util`): forked from
  [opencode](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode) (MIT).
- Agent kernel, from [pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi) by
  Mario Zechner (MIT), snapshot `f8f75544b` (2026-07-13):
  - `@earendil-works/pi-ai` is consumed as an npm dependency.
  - `packages/agent`: derived from pi `packages/agent` (the v1
    `AgentHarness` line), substantially modified and maintained here.
  - `packages/coding-agent`: the built-in tools (`read`/`bash`/`edit`/
    `write`, `edit-diff`, `path-utils`, `file-mutation-queue`),
    `core/system-prompt.ts` and `core/resources.ts` derive from pi
    `packages/coding-agent`; the embedded-debugging tools, toolchain,
    examples index and the ACP adapter are Yoma's own
    (see `packages/coding-agent/UPSTREAM.md`).
- `engines/stm32-config-kernel`: STM32 configuration / codegen kernel.
  `data/*.irpack` is a **build artifact**: parse the local STM32CubeMX
  device database with `stm32ck-import` (`bun engines/build.ts` does this).
  Packs are not committed. ST HAL / CMSIS sources (`data/fw/`, ~1.1GB)
  are also not in this repository; fetch them locally with
  `tools/fetch-fw.ps1` if you need the compile-gate tests.
- `engines/controller_map`: board netlist pin extraction.
- `packages/coding-agent/test/fixtures/examples/cube-mini`: a stub
  fixture that mimics an STM32Cube tree layout. It is not ST HAL source.

See `LICENSE` for the MIT text that covers this repository.
